<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia newspaper reports central bank scandal.</title>
<headline>Indonesia newspaper reports central bank scandal.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's central bank suffered seven billion rupiah ($2.9 million) in losses resulting from fake transactions, the Jakarta Post reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A Bank Indonesia spokeswoman confirmed the newspaper report but declined to give further details.</p>
<p>The bank's governor Sudradjat Djiwandono was quoted as saying on Monday about 5.4 billion rupiah of the seven billion rupiah had been recovered. The newspaper said it was the central bank's first public scandal in its 43-year history.</p>
<p>The paper said five people had been arrested and police were looking for two more suspects.</p>
<p>($1 = 2,341 rupiah)</p>
